Package: cudaFin
Type: Package
Title: GPU Rolling-Window Lasso Forecasting via the rcupp Framework
Version: 0.0.0.9008
Authors@R: person("Joe", "Zhu", email = "sha.joe.zhu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Joe Zhu [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Joe Zhu <sha.joe.zhu@gmail.com>
Description: A minimal downstream example of the 'rcupp' CUDA-for-Rcpp
    framework for finance-style workloads. Refits a lasso by ISTA on successive
    rolling windows of a feature matrix and produces one-step-ahead forecasts,
    using only rcupp's fixed GPU operators reached through LinkingTo: rcupp and
    R_GetCCallable(). It contains no CUDA code and no CUDA build logic of its
    own, and works identically whether rcupp was built with a CUDA backend or
    its CPU fallback. Intended as a template for rolling-window / portfolio
    signal workloads.
